From 7b175ebda85a8b98a1430db73513b9e97cb8bccb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:36:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] image_cache: honour the root preserveAspectRatio when
 rasterizing SVG images

An SVG drawn into a box whose aspect ratio differs from its own was scaled
non-uniformly to fill it, squashing e.g. discord.com's 165x24 header logo
in its 146x40 <img>. Chrome makes the box the document's viewport and fits
the viewBox into it with the root's preserveAspectRatio (meet letterboxes,
slice crops, alignments place the content), for <img>, CSS backgrounds and
inline <svg> alike. The rasterizer now parses the root viewBox and
preserveAspectRatio and maps the viewBox into the requested size, undoing
the fit usvg already applied for the document's own size. Documents
without a viewBox, or with preserveAspectRatio="none", still stretch, as
in Chrome.

Layout's approximation for inline <svg> (shrinking the content rect to the
natural aspect ratio and centring it) is removed: it only handled
"xMidYMid meet" and was wrong when width/height disagreed with the
viewBox.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
